    <briefdescription>
<para>Returns fractional area covered by water. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns the percent of water in a grid box.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>blon</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The longitude (in radians) at grid box boundaries. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>blat</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The latitude (in radians) at grid box boundaries. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">water_frac</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The fractional amount (0 to 1) of water in a grid box. The size of this field must be size(blon)-1 by size(blat)-1.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A logical value of TRUE is returned if the output field was successfully created. A value of FALSE may be returned if the Navy 1/6 degree percent water data set was not readable.</para></simplesect>
<linebreak/>
Example usage:<linebreak/>
<programlisting filename=".F90"><codeline><highlight class="normal">flag<sp/>=<sp/>get_water_frac(<sp/>blon,<sp/>blat,<sp/>water_frac<sp/>)<sp/></highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
